-- title:
--   Floor place under a maximal ideal of the jmatĥ-chart, q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix the prime $q$ together with the hypothesis $q = 2$, a level $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, with $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ and $\mathrm{jNGeomGen}$ in the valuation ring, and value of $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$), let $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the floor field along $A$ whose residue map is computed coefficientwise on Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ ($hR_0$). Further data: an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; an index $\zeta$; families $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the line $\mathrm{lineInfty}$ consists of the ratios $x/y$ of Laurent series over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction, each $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the pullback of that ring along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ carrying $\mathrm{lineInfty}$ to $\ell$, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, and permutation of the family by all $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contracts to $A$ on constants, is invariant under all these automorphisms, contains an element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit for every $a \in A$, and lies over $s$ in the sense that any $f$ in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ at every place $P$ where $\mathrm{jq}$ has nonnegative order and with $R_0$-reduction in the valuation ring of $s$ maps into $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, with $f - a$ in the maximal ideal whenever $a \in A$ reduces to $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that reduction. Descent data: a subfield $K_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ over which $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is algebraic, with $\pi \in K_0$; a henselian discrete valuation domain $A_0$ with an injective local homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image is $A \cap K_0$, with $\mathrm{residue} \circ \iota$ surjective, with maximal ideal generated by $\varpi_0$ and $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$; the subfield $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of elements all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$, containing the image $\hat\jmath$ of $\mathrm{jq}$, which is nonzero, with an $A_0$-algebra structure induced by $\iota$; and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak n$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,F_0\,\hat\jmath$, the subalgebra of elements of $F_0$ integral over $A_0[\hat\jmath]$, containing the image of $\varpi_0$. The conclusion: there is a place $s$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ which is rational, satisfies $\mathrm{IsAffineGeomPlace}$, and over which $\mathfrak n$ lies, namely: for every $f$ in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of nonnegative order at every place where $\mathrm{jq}$ has nonnegative order and with $R_0$-reduction in the valuation ring of $s$, and every $a \in A_0$ whose image $\iota(a)$ reduces to $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that reduction, every $g$ in the chart algebra whose image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ equals $f - \iota(a)$ lies in $\mathfrak n$; and for every $a \in A_0$ with $\iota(a)$ reducing to $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})$, the element $\mathrm{jChartFin} - a$ lies in $\mathfrak n$.
--
--   This is the point-to-place dictionary for the descended two-chart integral model in the case $q = 2$: a maximal ideal of the $\hat\jmath$-finite chart containing the uniformiser determines a rational affine place of the reduced level-$M'$ modular function field over the residue field of $A$, compatibly with the constant reduction $R_0$ and with the value of $\hat\jmath$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_ssPlace_floorTrace_of_isMaximal_chartAlgFin_of_mem_ssJSet_descent_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_ssPlace_floorTrace_of_isMaximal_chartAlgFin_of_mem_ssJSet_descent_of_eq_two), which identifies the resulting place as a supersingular one.
